    "body": "https://sideshowbarker.net/html-syntax-highlight/#parsing-an-event-stream shouldn't have highlighting (or use an ABNF highlighter).\r\n\r\nI'm not sure about the highlighting in IDL blocks using JS, that seems bogus.\r\n\r\nSome things are mis-highlighted as CSS:\r\n\r\nhttps://sideshowbarker.net/html-syntax-highlight/#the-head-element\r\nhttps://sideshowbarker.net/html-syntax-highlight/#introduction-13\r\nhttps://sideshowbarker.net/html-syntax-highlight/#communicating-with-a-dedicated-worker\r\nhttps://sideshowbarker.net/html-syntax-highlight/#the-workernavigator-object\r\n\r\n(I didn't check all instances, so the above might not be exhaustive.)\r\n\r\nWe may want to not have any highlighting in https://sideshowbarker.net/html-syntax-highlight/#parse-errors and other intentionally-invalid examples, since the highlighter doesn't follow HTML's rules, it's rather adding confusion. (Maybe this could be achieved by adding the `bad` class to these.)\r\n\r\nMaybe the background color should be the same when the script runs as when it doesn't?\r\n\r\nDo we want the colors to match between this and `.domTree`?",
