    "body": "> Some things are mis-highlighted as CSS:\r\n\r\nWe could handle those by either putting `class=\"nohighlight\"` on then in `source`, or else `class=\"javascript\"` or whatever it they actually really are.\r\n\r\n> We may want to not have any highlighting in https://sideshowbarker.net/html-syntax-highlight/#parse-errors and other intentionally-invalid examples, since the highlighter doesn't follow HTML's rules, it's rather adding confusion. (Maybe this could be achieved by adding the `bad` class to these.)\r\n\r\nWe could add `class=\"nohighlight\"` on those \r\n\r\nSee https://highlightjs.org/usage/",
