    "updated_at": "2017-06-12T20:54:04Z",
    "body": "The alternative here is adding a Node.js or Python step to the build process which post-processes ahead of time (since none of us want to write a syntax highlighter in Free Pascal). I'm a little wary about adding more script to initial page load, especially for single-page.\r\n\r\nBut going with a runtime version seems OK for now, as long as it doesn't jank singlepage too much. (And even that could probably be fixed upstream with judicious requestIdleCallback/fallback-to-setTimeout usage.)\r\n\r\n\"do not merge yet\" since we need to update the URLs and accept the relevant PRs elsewhere. Although I think since this is HTML-specific having it in this repository (or html-build??) seems reasonable...",
