    "body": "> We could handle those by either putting `class=\"nohighlight\"` on then in `source`, or else `class=\"javascript\"` or whatever it they actually really are.\r\n\r\nFWIW, Highlight.js supports [the convention](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/text-level-semantics.html#the-code-element) documented in the HTML Standard itself, i.e. `class=language-javascript` (instead of `class=javascript`).\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">…</code></pre>\r\n```",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
