    "updated_at": "2017-06-12T21:12:19Z",
    "body": "Probably for the same reason we just use `pre` in the CSS specs - `<pre><code>` makes the magical-newline-omitting of `pre` work even worse than `pre` by itself.\r\n\r\n> The alternative here is adding a Node.js or Python step to the build process which post-processes ahead of time (since none of us want to write a syntax highlighter in Free Pascal).\r\n\r\nI've got some decent code for Python already in Bikeshed, using the pretty-good Pygments library.  It properly preserves markup in the original code, too, which a lot of highlighters don't do.",
